NAME
     ln - make links between files

SYNOPSIS
     ln [-s] TARGET NAME

DESCRIPTION
     ln makes NAME another name for TARGET: a hard link, which is the
     same inode under two names, or with -s a symbolic link, which is a
     small file holding the path to follow.

OPTIONS
     -s   make a symbolic link rather than a hard one

SEE ALSO
     ls(1), stat(1), readlink(1)
